#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Native packages first, then Flatpak, then AUR — and why Ditana ships Brave from AUR rather than Flathub."
msgstr "L’emprim pachets nativs, lura Flatpak, lura AUR – e pertge che Ditana furnescha Brave dad AUR e betg da Flathub."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUR vs Flatpak"
msgstr "AUR u Flatpak"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"Ditana supports native Arch packages, AUR packages built locally with "
"`paru`, and Flatpak applications sandboxed from Flathub. The priority "
"sequence is **native first, followed by Flatpak, then AUR** – and the "
"justification for moving beyond a native package is never that Flatpak "
"offers better experience, but that no native package is available."
msgstr ""
"Ditana sustegna pachets nativs dad Arch, pachets AUR construids localmain "
"cun `paru` ed applicaziuns Flatpak da Flathub isoladas en in sandbox. "
"L’urden da prioritad è **l’emprim nativ, lura Flatpak, alura AUR** – ed il "
"motiv da tscherner insatge auter ch’in pachet nativ n’è mai che Flatpak "
"porschia ina meglra experientscha, mabain ch’i n’è disponibel nagin pachet "
"nativ."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "When Flatpak is the better choice"
msgstr "Cura che Flatpak è la meglra tscherna"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"When Arch itself does not carry a package, favour Flatpak over the AUR for a "
"desktop application that has a maintained Flathub build."
msgstr ""
"Sche Arch sez n’ha betg in pachet, preferi Flatpak a l’AUR per "
"in’applicaziun da desktop che ha in build mantegnì sin Flathub."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"**Sandboxing.** Flatpak applications run in a `bubblewrap` sandbox with "
"restricted filesystem and IPC access. For browsers, media players, and other "
"internet-facing software, this is a real defence-in-depth layer."
msgstr ""
"**Isolaziun en in sandbox.** Las applicaziuns Flatpak vegnan exequidas en in "
"sandbox `bubblewrap` cun in access limità al sistem da datotecas ed a l’IPC. "
"Per navigaturs, programs da multimedia ed autra software exponida a "
"l’internet è quai ina vaira stresa supplementara da protecziun."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"**No build time.** AUR packages built from source can take minutes (or "
"hours, for large applications like LibreOffice). Flatpak deployments "
"download pre-built binaries from Flathub."
msgstr ""
"**Nagin temp da build.** Il build da pachets AUR dal code da funtauna po "
"durar minutas (u uras, per grondas applicaziuns sco LibreOffice). "
"Installaziuns cun Flatpak telechargian datotecas binaras gia cumpiladas da "
"Flathub."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"**No ABI risk.** Binary AUR packages occasionally break when system "
"libraries are updated and the upstream binary expects a different ABI. "
"Flatpaks bundle their runtime and are insulated from that risk."
msgstr ""
"**Nagin ristg d’ABI.** Pachets AUR binars na funcziunan mintgatant betg pli, "
"cura che bibliotecas dal sistem vegnan actualisadas e la datoteca binara "
"d’origin spetga in’autra ABI. Ils Flatpaks cuntegnan lur agen runtime ed èn "
"protegids cunter quest ristg."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"**Predictable updates.** Flathub releases are versioned and easy to roll "
"back. AUR is rolling and uncoordinated."
msgstr ""
"**Actualisaziuns previsiblas.** Sin Flathub ha mintga versiun in numer da "
"versiun, ed ins po facilmain turnar ad ina versiun precedenta. AUR sa mida "
"cuntinuadamain e senza coordinaziun."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "When AUR is the better choice"
msgstr "Cura che AUR è la meglra tscherna"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"There are three cases where Ditana prefers — or requires — AUR over Flatpak."
msgstr ""
"I dat trais cas nua che Ditana preferescha – u pretenda – AUR empè da "
"Flatpak."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"Ditana already rebuilds and signs 45 of the AUR recipes it needs, so `paru "
"-S` will often resolve them from the Ditana repository rather than from the "
"AUR. Every one of those was classified before it was built: a change to a "
"source URL, to a build function, or to a checksum without a version stops "
"the whole run for a person to look at. Recipes Ditana does not carry are "
"installed by `paru` straight from the AUR, unreviewed, which is the "
"difference the rest of this page is about."
msgstr ""
"Ditana reconstruescha e signa gia 45 dals recepts da l’AUR che la "
"distribuziun dovra, uschia che `paru -S` chatta quels savens en il "
"repositori da Ditana e betg en l’AUR. Mintgin da quels è vegnì classifitgà "
"avant il build: ina midada da l’URL d’ina funtauna, d’ina funcziun da build "
"u d’ina summa da controlla senza nova versiun ferma l’entira execuziun, per "
"ch’ina persuna examineschia la midada. Recepts che Ditana n’ha betg vegnan "
"installads da `paru` directamain da l’AUR, senza revisiun – e quai è la "
"differenza da la quala tracta il rest da questa pagina."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chromium-based browsers under Ditana's default hardening"
msgstr "Navigaturs sin basa da Chromium cun il rinforzament da standard da Ditana"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"Ditana does not hand unprivileged user namespaces to each program. They have "
"formed the basis of several published local privilege escalations, and of "
"the sixteen Linux kernel entries in CISA’s [Known Exploited Vulnerabilities "
"catalogue](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog) "
"over three years, six are exploitable via them – counted against catalogue "
"version 2026.09.04, and the reading of which six is ours, so it is worth "
"checking rather than believing. Ditana therefore allows them on a per-"
"program basis: a minimal BPF program attached to the kernel’s own "
"`userns_create` hook refuses a namespace to any executable that a setting "
"has not requested. `bwrap` has requested it, so every Flatpak builds its "
"outer sandbox as usual."
msgstr ""
"Ditana na dat betg spazis da num da l’utilisader senza privilegis a mintga "
"program. Els èn stads la basa da pliras escalaziuns da privilegis localas "
"publitgadas, e da las sedesch endataziuns dal kernel Linux en il [Known "
"Exploited Vulnerabilities catalogue](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-"
"vulnerabilities-catalog) da CISA durant trais onns èn sis explotablas cun "
"agid da quels – dumbrà tenor la versiun dal catalog 2026.09.04; la "
"valitaziun, da tge sis endataziuns ch’i sa tracta, è nossa, perquai vala la "
"paina da la verifitgar empè da la crair. Perquai permetta Ditana quels "
"spazis da num program per program: in program BPF minimal, collià cun il "
"hook `userns_create` dal kernel sez, refusa in spazi da num a mintga program "
"exequibel per il qual nagin parameter n’ha dumandà quai. `bwrap` ha dumandà "
"quai, uschia che mintga Flatpak construescha ses sandbox extern sco usità."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"Brave nevertheless comes from the AUR as `brave-bin`, for two reasons that "
"have nothing to do with the outer sandbox. Its Flatpak carries `zypak`, "
"which establishes additional namespaces from a binary of its own deep inside "
"the sandbox, and whether a per-executable allowlist extends to those at all "
"is untested. And an executable within a Flatpak is replaced by `flatpak "
"update`, which the hook responsible for maintaining the allowlist in sync "
"does not see, so the permission would silently expire on the next update."
msgstr ""
"Brave vegn tuttina da l’AUR sco `brave-bin`, per dus motivs che n’han nagut "
"da far cun il sandbox extern. Ses Flatpak cuntegna `zypak`, che creescha "
"spazis da num supplementars a partir d’in’atgna datoteca binara situada en "
"la profunditad dal sandbox, e sch’ina glista da permissiuns per program "
"exequibel vala insumma er per quels, n’è betg testà. Ultra da quai remplazza "
"`flatpak update` in program exequibel en in Flatpak, ed il hook responsabel "
"per tegnair sincronisada la glista da permissiuns na vesa betg quai; uschia "
"scadess la permissiun tacitamain a la proxima actualisaziun."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"The AUR package `brave-bin` needs none of this. It brings its own setuid "
"`chrome-sandbox` helper and builds its sandbox without a user namespace at "
"all – which is why this one remains in place even though the rule puts "
"Flatpak ahead of the AUR."
msgstr ""
"Il pachet AUR `brave-bin` na dovra nagut da quai. El porta ses agen program "
"d’agid setuid `chrome-sandbox` e construescha ses sandbox dal tuttafatg "
"senza spazi da num da l’utilisader – perquai resta quest pachet, schebain "
"che la regla metta Flatpak avant l’AUR."

#. type: Title ####
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a sandbox you installed yourself is refused"
msgstr "Sch’in sandbox installà da Vus vegn refusà"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"If a sandbox you installed yourself is refused a user namespace, the guard "
"is what refused it. Add the executable to `/etc/ditana/userns-allow.conf`, "
"one absolute path per line, and reload:"
msgstr ""
"Sch’in sandbox installà da Vus na survegn nagin spazi da num da "
"l’utilisader, è il guardian quel che ha refusà il spazi da num. Agiuntai il "
"program exequibel a `/etc/ditana/userns-allow.conf`, in percurs absolut per "
"lingia, e rechargiai la configuraziun:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo ditana-userns-guard --reload\n"
msgstr "sudo ditana-userns-guard --reload\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"`sudo ditana-userns-guard --status` shows how many namespaces have been "
"permitted and refused since the guard was loaded, and lists the programs it "
"refused, the most recent first, each with the user who ran it and how often. "
"`sudo ditana-userns-guard --observe` stops refusing and keeps the list, so "
"it shows what a program would ask for while the program keeps running; `sudo "
"ditana-userns-guard` switches refusing back on."
msgstr ""
"`sudo ditana-userns-guard --status` mussa quants spazis da num ch’èn vegnids "
"permess e refusads dapi ch’il guardian è vegnì chargià, ed enumerescha ils "
"programs ch’el ha refusà, ils pli recents l’emprim, mintgin cun l’account "
"d’utilisader che l’ha exequì e cun il dumber da las giadas. `sudo ditana-"
"userns-guard --observe` chala da refusar e mantegna la glista, uschia ch’el "
"mussa tge ch’in program dumandass, entant ch’il program cuntinuescha a "
"funcziunar; `sudo ditana-userns-guard` activescha puspè il refus."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Software not available on Flathub"
msgstr "Software che n’è betg disponibla sin Flathub"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"A non-trivial fraction of useful Linux software lives only on AUR — niche "
"developer tools, vendor-specific drivers, hardware utilities, fonts. For "
"these, AUR is the only option, and `paru` makes installing them "
"straightforward."
msgstr ""
"Ina part betg negligibla da la software Linux utila sa chatta mo sin AUR – "
"utensils da svilup spezialisads, drivers specifics d’in fabricant, programs "
"d’agid per la hardware, scrittiras. En quests cas è AUR l’unica opziun, e "
"cun `paru` è lur installaziun simpla."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you want to participate in the AUR ecosystem"
msgstr "Cura che Vus vulais participar a l’ecosistem AUR"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"If you're an Arch user who wants to follow AUR commit feeds, contribute "
"votes, or maintain your own AUR packages, sticking with AUR for daily "
"applications keeps you in that loop."
msgstr ""
"Sche Vus utilisais Arch e vulais suandar ils feeds da commits da l’AUR, "
"votar per pachets u mantegnair Voss agens pachets AUR, alura As tegna "
"l’utilisaziun dad AUR per las applicaziuns da mintga di en contact cun quest "
"ecosistem."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How Ditana decides at install time"
msgstr "Co che Ditana decida durant l’installaziun"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"The KDL configuration lets each setting declare `arch-packages`, `flatpak-"
"packages` and `aur-packages` side by side, and `userns-allow` for an "
"executable whose sandbox needs a user namespace. When more than one source "
"is available, the choice is made deliberately, package by package, with an "
"explanation recorded in the relevant `.kdl` file. Browse [ditana-config]"
"(https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config) to see the reasoning in context."
msgstr ""
"La configuraziun KDL permetta a mintga parameter da declerar `arch-"
"packages`, `flatpak-packages` ed `aur-packages` l’in sper l’auter, sco er "
"`userns-allow` per in program exequibel che dovra in spazi da num da "
"l’utilisader per ses sandbox. Sche pli ch’ina funtauna è disponibla, vegn la "
"tscherna fatga cun intenziun, pachet per pachet, cun in’explicaziun "
"registrada en la datoteca `.kdl` correspundenta. Consultai [ditana-config]"
"(https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config) per vesair l’argumentaziun en ses "
"context."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Practical tip: review installed Flatpaks regularly"
msgstr "Cussegl pratic: controllar regularmain ils Flatpaks installads"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/best-practices/aur-vs-flatpak.md
msgid ""
"Flatpak runtimes accumulate. Run `sudo flatpak uninstall --unused` "
"occasionally to reclaim disk space – and `sudo flatpak update` to keep "
"applications current. Both are safe operations. Ditana installs Flatpaks "
"into the system installation rather than a per-user one, which is why both "
"need root."
msgstr ""
"Ils runtimes da Flatpak s’accumuleschan. Exequi mintgatant `sudo flatpak "
"uninstall --unused` per liberar spazi sin il disc – e `sudo flatpak update` "
"per tegnair actualas las applicaziuns. Omaduas èn operaziuns segiras. Ditana "
"installescha ils Flatpaks en l’installaziun dal sistem e betg en ina "
"installaziun per account d’utilisader, perquai dovran omaduas privilegis da "
"root."
